def all_unique(items):
    seen = set()
    for item in items:
        if item in seen:
            return False
        seen.add(item)
    return True
```

This function now correctly checks if all items in the input list are unique. It iterates over the input list, adding each item to a set. If it encounters an item that is already in the set, it immediately returns False, indicating that not all items are unique. If it iterates over the entire list without finding any duplicate items, it returns True, indicating that all items are unique.
